          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best cordless vacuum for hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The Dyson V12 Detect Slim Absolute is the best cordless vacuum for hardwood floors for most people who can afford it. Its laser makes invisible dust visible on hard floors, and it counts particles on screen as you clean. The Shark Detect Pro is the better value, with automatic floor, dirt and edge detection and sealed HEPA filtration.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a cordless vacuum good for hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. Hardwood needs less power than carpet, so a cordless stick's battery goes further on bare floors. Light weight also makes it easy to do quick daily passes, which keeps grit from scratching the finish. Choose one with headlights or dust detection, sealed filtration and a brushroll that slows or adjusts on hard floors.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a vacuum scratch hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It can if grit gets trapped under the head or wheels, or if a stiff brushroll spins fast on a soft finish. Check the underside of the head regularly, keep the wheels free of hair, and use a vacuum that slows its brushroll on hard floors. Vacuuming often actually protects floors by removing abrasive grit.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you use a wet-dry vacuum on hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                On sealed hardwood with an intact finish, yes, using the lowest water setting that cleans the mess. Wet-dry vacuums like the Tineco Floor ONE S5 pick water up in the same pass. Do not use them on unsealed, waxed or worn floors, and check your flooring warranty for any restrictions.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I turn off the brushroll on hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                On many vacuums a slower or stopped brushroll works better on hardwood, because fast stiff bristles scatter debris. Floor-sensing vacuums like the Shark Detect Pro and PowerPro Reveal Plus adjust brushroll speed automatically. If yours has a manual setting for hard floors, use it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How often should you vacuum hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                In busy homes or homes with pets, a quick pass daily or every other day in high-traffic areas, plus a fuller clean weekly. Frequent vacuuming removes grit before it is ground into the finish, which is the main cause of dull, scratched hardwood.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best cheap cordless vacuum for hardwood floors?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The Levoit LVAC-200 is the best budget pick. It lies flat to reach under furniture, has LED lights to show dust, an anti-tangle brush and filtration listed at 99.9 percent of particles down to 0.3 microns. Expect about 30 minutes with the floor head, per the listing, and filter changes every three months.
              </p>
            </div>

